# A Gaussian beam spreads as w0 sqrt(1 + (z / z_R)^2); the paraxial equation reproduces this exactly.
# Reference: the closed form, within 0.4% (grid and window).
title Gaussian beam of 3 um waist diffracting in the cladding
grid dx=0.05 dz=0.25
window width=276 length=200
launch gaussian x=0 radius=3
plane end z=200
expect total end 1.000000000 2e-7
expect centroid end -0.0000000 2e-6
expect radius end 22.9715019 2e-6
expect neff 1.443190083 2e-8
expect radius end 22.97511 0.0919
expect conserved 1e-6
expect centroid end 0 1e-6
